{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"suave-constant-cow","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Abort a stalled review-bot `git fetch` in seconds instead of burning the 300s budget\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nBug `df2c-e4b8-496d-4698` proved that the review bot's per-review `git fetch` of the GitHub\nmirror intermittently hangs: 25 consecutive runs inside `compose-review-bot-1` produced 2\nhangs past 320s (rc=124) against a 1-3s median on an 80 MB / 54k-object repo. The bot's git\nhas no `http.lowSpeedLimit` / `http.lowSpeedTime` and no keepalive, so a stalled connection\nconsumes the whole `_GIT_TIMEOUT = 300` (`src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:295`) before\n`_fetch_origin` gives up. `df2c` removes the DURABLE damage (the stall no longer becomes an\n`LLM-Review -1`); it does not shorten the stall. A review still burns 5 minutes and is only\nrecovered on the next backfill pass.\n\n## Approach\n\nConfigure the review bot's git so a dead connection aborts in seconds, and/or retry the fetch\nin-process a bounded number of times inside the existing timeout budget, so a transient stall\ncosts seconds rather than five minutes and usually self-heals within the same review.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A stalled fetch aborts in single-digit seconds rather than at the 300s ceiling,\n      demonstrated by a reproduction against an unresponsive remote.\n- [ ] A transient stall is retried in-process so the common case still produces a real\n      review rather than an abstain.\n- [ ] A genuinely slow-but-progressing fetch is not aborted (the low-speed threshold is\n      keyed on throughput, not wall time).","id":"12e4-8c74-a738-4014","parent_id":"061c-ecd1-8967-4a76","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"review-bot: abort a stalled git fetch in seconds instead of burning the 300s timeout"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785706683006342001,"uuid":"136c03c6-3889-4b47-bec9-f361d9cf240c"}